"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As it's impossible to decrease numbers, we have to increase them to at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"). If all the numbers are already equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") then there is no need to increase any of them as it will cost extra operations. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So you should find "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") using one iteration over the array. Then iterate one more time summing up differences between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" and maximum. And the answer is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/106f15076a2e9a654ca14e00b69a9e4853b98faa837a7d4f1b69fd352887ee7d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"758B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/758/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"758B - Blown Garland"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Four consecutive bulbs should not be of the same color, and it is four possible colors, so the color of the fifth bulb is the same as the first bulb has, the color of the sixth is the same as the second bulb has, it means that the color of the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bulb equals the color of the ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 4)-th bulb. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the coordinates of all bulbs of the same color equal in module 4. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"According to the conditions of the problem the coordinate of at least one light bulb of each color is given, so we can restore the garland and by one pass count the number of blown bulbs. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"By one pass we learn how numbers in module 4 correspond to the colors. By the second pass we know the place of the bulb and count the number of blown bulbs of each color. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The asymptotic behavior of the solutions is  — O(n)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is also a second solution:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can just fix order of first four light bulbs by bruteforce (there is only 4! = 24 variants), checking the conformity of each option of the given garland. By finding the color of the first four bulbs we easily recreate the garland with working lights and count the number of blown bulbs. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At worst this decision will work for 24·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Kniaz"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kniaz"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"758C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/758/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"758C - Unfair Poll"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's learn to count "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of questions which were asked to the pupil in the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th row, at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th place in the order. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the process of asking is periodic. During one period children were asked in the following order: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the first row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the first row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the first row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the first row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the ... row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the ... row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the first table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the second table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the ... table; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the pupil from the second row who seats at the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" table. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" The next the pupil from the first row who seats at the first table, the period starts from the beginning. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, during one period "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 2)·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" pupils who seats at the outer rows will be asked once, others will be asked twice. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1, then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The number of full periods equals "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/ea1942696477b519b5757d5b25ee73cc90fbc2cebe02852851631538167dbffe.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". The remaining questions are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"mod"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"  ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so we can only make poll on the remaining questions for the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or for individual "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" print the formula. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") can be seen as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On what places are people who may be asked more times than the other? Firstly, this is the first row and the first table, because the poll begins from it. Secondly, this is the second row and the first table, because the poll of the central, not outer part of a class at the right side, begins from it. Thirdly, the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 row and the first place because the poll of the central, not outer part of a class at the left side, begins from it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The maximum number of asked questions to one pupil equals "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"max"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1, 1), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(2, 1), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, 1))."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The minimum number of asked questions to one pupil equals "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"f"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), because the pupil who seats on the last row and at the last table will be asked less than others. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, we have decisions with the asymptotic "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(1)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Kniaz"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kniaz"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"758D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/758/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"758D - Ability To Convert"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's compare answers for numbers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/c97104d38c019080277ba904175d1af9f39ed751a57829d089c0d91cc8cd3734.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" without the rightmost digit."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that for any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" number "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/438f115dc767d407c6973540914fa4d2fbe0c230aa1a6e0341fc94dc54e6c68c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" is either contains less substrings (valid digits in base-"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" numeric system) or it's possible to decrease value of the last substring of number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That proves that partition of number without the rightmost digit isn't worse than partition of the number itself. Thus, greedy strategy will work. On each step take the longest suffix of a string as the last base-"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" digit and proceed to same task for string with this suffix excluded. Repeat until the string isn't empty."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Check carefully that the suffix is a number less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and also doesn't have any leading zeros except for the case when it's equal to zero."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity — "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — length of input string. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Problem author: "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/MikeMirzayanov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"MikeMirzayanov"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/Kniaz"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Kniaz"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"758E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/758/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"758E - Broken Tree"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, let's calculate min and max weight for subtrees of each vertex."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Minimal weight of a subtree is sum of minimal weights of all adjacent to the root of current subtree subtrees and sum of weights of all outgoing edges reduced in weight to minimal possible."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, minimal weight is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/8e4e7f944b85ec82b7a37af5f4c17c99ddd1199d5e989d32c86ca3c909f23c49.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" —subtree root, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" —number of outgoing edges from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — each adjacent to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertex, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — its strength, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — its weight."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that minimal weight should be less or equal to strength of incoming edge. If this condition isn't satisfied for at least one subtree then the answer is  - 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Maximal weight of a subtree is sum of maximal weights of all adjacent to the root of current subtree subtrees and sum of weights of all outgoing edges. Note that this maximum should stay in such boundaries that the tree remains unbroken. So maximal weight should not exceed strength of incoming edge of a root."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Therefore, maximum is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/01d9439bda86bf3e1d1821b19d68121fbfa31955deb99b31cfc0e954c2f6fd81.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" —subtree root, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — weight of an incoming edge of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", that is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th edge outgoing from some vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"z"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" —number of outgoing edges from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" — each adjacent to "},{"chil