"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One dfs from the root of the tree is enough to calculate all these values."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpmin"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpmax"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpW"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" are set to 0 for leaves ."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpmax"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" is maximal possible weight of each subtree, so weight of the whole tree can be reduced to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpmax"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":", it means that weight of subtree of vertex 1 should be reduced by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpW"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dpmax"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Next goal is to learn how to reduce weight of subtree of vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" units. At first, you should reduce weights of subtrees of adjacent to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertices to their maximum. So after this step "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/29b28d543de85927e067b76eed4c2a5bc013fd6a1a96f28f8266e3ca29483079.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then 